   $ 5 \text{ shelves} \times 4 \text{ books per shelf} = 20 \text{ books} $.
3. **Calculate the number of picture books:**  
   $ 3 \text{ shelves} \times 4 \text{ books per shelf} = 12 \text{ books} $.
4. **Add both quantities together:**  
   $ 20 \text{ mystery books} + 12 \text{ picture books} = 32 \text{ books} $.
5. **Final Answer:**  
   $\boxed{32}$  
